  "problem": "Captured CMS/CDC/Census documents mixed CSV, XLSX, text-PDF and painted-grid families. Unsupported, scanned, encrypted and ambiguous layouts could be treated as payload success, and PDF window checkpoints could be reused after source or extractor bytes changed.",
  "resulting_behavior": "collect-pdf-windows.mjs now exports routeDocument. CSV (parseTextCodebook), XLSX (parseWorkbookCells), text-PDF (parseCmsDictionary or captured pypdf 6.18.0 windows) and grid (parseGrid) are selected only from validated format/layout evidence. Unsupported, scanned, encrypted, missing-source, ambiguous-layout and parser-defect documents remain residual with payload_success and publication_authorized false. resumeDocumentWindows merges mid-document PDF windows without lost or duplicate pages and invalidates checkpoints when pdf_sha256 or extractor_sha256 change. buildDocumentExtractionCoverage groups those residual reasons without live source traffic. The CLI remains gated. Live fetch is forbidden. Parser routing lives in the owned collect-pdf-windows.mjs path; no extra unowned helper remains.",
